        {
          "post_id": "507876",
          "text": "<p>The sequence $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ is an optimal non-preemptive scheduling sequence for the following jobs which leaves the CPU idle for $\\_\\_\\_\\_$ unit(s) of time.</p><p>\\[<br>\\begin{array}{c|c|c}<br>\\text{Job} & \\text{Arrival Time} & \\text{Burst Time} \\\\<br>\\hline<br>1 & 0.0 & 4 \\\\<br>2 & 1.5 & 8 \\\\<br>3 & 2.0 & 2<br>\\end{array}<br>\\]</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$\\{1,3,2\\}, 0$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\{1,2,3\\}, 0$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\{3,1,2\\}, 2$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\{1,3,2\\}, 1.5$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Operating System",
          "day": "Day 168"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "507883",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following set of CPU-intensive processes. The operating system uses the <strong>Preemptive Shortest Remaining Time First (SRTF)</strong> scheduling algorithm.</p><p>\\[<br>\\begin{array}{c|c|c}<br>\\text{Process} & \\text{Arrival Time} & \\text{Burst Time} \\\\<br>\\hline<br>\\text{P1} & 0 & 8 \\\\<br>\\text{P2} & 2 & 3 \\\\<br>\\text{P3} & 5 & 2 \\\\<br>\\text{P4} & 6 & 4<br>\\end{array}<br>\\]<br>Find the <strong>Average Turnaround Time </strong>and the number of <strong>Context Switches</strong> (excluding the switch at time zero and at the very end).</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>Avg TAT $: 6.50$; Context Switches $: 4$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>Avg TAT $:&nbsp;6.75$; Context Switches $: 3$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>Avg TAT $: 6.75$; Context Switches $: 4$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>Avg TAT$: 7.50$; Context Switches $: 3$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Operating System",
          "day": "Day 168"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "507896",
          "text": "<p>Consider a system where a CPU generates $\\mathbf{32-}$<strong>bit virtual addresses</strong> with a <strong>page size of</strong> $\\mathbf{8 ~KB}$. The system has a $\\mathbf{2-way}$ <strong>set associative TLB</strong> that can hold $\\mathbf{256}$<strong> page table entries.</strong></p><p>Calculate the <strong>minimum size of the TLB tag</strong></p>",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "12",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Operating System",
          "day": "Day 168"
        },
        {
